  "findings": [
    "WPF and the production helper compiled; 155 host controls and 91 packaged-helper protocol checks passed.",
    "The native window scenario completed 63 checks. It passed normal row sizing, workspace pane toggles, capture refusal, splitter and fader bounds, ordinary editing, and the CPR review/import journey, then timed out at source-auto-expand during source-event-ui-selection.",
    "The recorded Normal geometry is 68-DIP rows, 298-DIP track-content bottom and 327-DIP viewport height. The previous normal-density failure is not reproduced in this candidate.",
    "Eight workspace states retain the same shared-session hash and revision. Hiding both panes produces a 565-DIP timeline viewport; the splitter reached mixer heights 196 and 340 with a 220-DIP minimum arrangement and preserved keyboard focus.",
    "The retained geometry also reports eight DIP of vertical scroll range in the default, normal and restored layouts despite the four tracks fitting. Those original measurements are preserved; this record does not promote the workspace to final visual acceptance.",
    "Source-level diagnosis found that the smoke selected the current track, whose ProjectSelection.selectingTrack behavior preserves the current source event. Reassigning that event is ignored by the host same-ID guard, so the test did not create the selection transition its auto-expansion expectation required. This is a code-derived explanation, not additional runtime state instrumentation.",
    "Five PNGs were emitted: normal and expanded workspace views, the source-selection failure view, and both CPR review sizes. Final main/source/scroll captures were not reached. The two CPR PNGs are byte-identical to the earlier accepted captures.",
    "The source-only ordinary-action refusal check passed, but the aggregate source-only receipt remained null because it is populated after the failed auto-expansion wait. Source attachment/export and the subsequent native ruler/scroll journey were not reached.",
    "The application workflow shared Release gate and ZIP assembly were not reached. The successful 13-job component run is retained separately.",
    "All 16 packaged-helper CPR gates and exact example/source PCM, waveform and ruler locks matched the separate component results. The standalone native adapter passed 89 lifecycle checks; both endpoint observations reported unavailable, with no playback measured."
